What carried over and what did not
----------------------------------

* The source code, the NexusMods.* project and namespace names, and the
  developer notes under docs/developers are upstream's, kept so changes can
  be merged across. Their names are provenance, not a claim to the brand.
* Artwork that Nexus Mods wrote and that stays in the tree (placeholder
  images, pictograms) comes with the GPL-3.0-only code it shipped in. The
  license covers the files, not the Nexus Mods trademarks. The Nexus Mods
  logos and glyphs were removed.
* erm, the author's earlier project, is GPL-2.0-or-later. Code brought
  over from it is used here under GPL-3.0-only, which its "or later" clause
  allows.
* NexusMods.MnemonicDB (https://github.com/Nexus-Mods/NexusMods.MnemonicDB, tag v0.28.2, GPL-3.0-only),
  the database library the app stores its data in, is vendored as source under
  src/NexusMods.MnemonicDB*. It was a NuGet package before; the databases it
  wrote still open unchanged. Its license is in src/NexusMods.MnemonicDB/LICENSE.
* The docs theme submodule (NexusMods.MkDocsMaterial.Themes.Next, GPL-3.0)
  was dropped along with the documentation site it built. Its license text
  is the GPL, the same as this project's.
* Data from an installed Nexus Mods App is not imported. SilverModManager
  keeps its own data directory and does not read upstream's.

Third-party components, fonts and icons, with their licenses, are listed in
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
